From whuber at embl.de  Sun Feb 20 15:32:59 2011
From: whuber at embl.de (Wolfgang Huber)
Date: Sun, 20 Feb 2011 15:32:59 +0100
Subject: [BioC] announcing a new version of arrayQualityMetrics in the
 development branch
Message-ID: <4D61261B.1060902@embl.de>

Hi,

a substantially revised version of arrayQualityMetrics is available.

It has a number of new features:
- improved interactivity of the plots; expandable/collapsible sections
- rationalised outlier detection and reporting
- friendlier handling of the dependence on svg (should now be 
transparent to most users, especially on Windows).

If you use the package, or want use it, it is worth installing the 
version from the devel branch, not from the last release, even on R 
2.12.x. If you use R-devel (the future R 2.13), then you can simply use 
biocLite to install it. If you use 2.12.x, go to 
http://www.bioconductor.org/help/bioc-views/devel/bioc/html/arrayQualityMetrics.html 
and download the package, install it, as well as those dependencies that 
you need.

A couple of example reports (from the package vignette) are here:
http://www-huber.embl.de/users/whuber/bioc-list/110220

Given the diversity of datasets and use cases that people have, I am 
sure there is still some scope for fine-tuning of the report 
presentation. I'd be very happy about any feedback on this, or any other 
matter.

Best wishes
Wolfgang Huber
EMBL
http://www.embl.de/research/units/genome_biology/huber


